---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { booneCameraInventorySummary, booneCameraInventoryTotals } from '../../../../data/deflock';
import CountyMunicipalityMap from '../../../../components/jurisdictions/CountyMunicipalityMap.astro';
import PublicRecords from '../../../../components/jurisdictions/PublicRecords.astro';
import { booneMunicipalities, booneMunicipalitySource } from '../../../../data/illinois/counties/boone';
import { booneCountyRecords } from '../../../../data/illinois/counties/boone-records';

---
<BaseLayout
  title="Boone County Surveillance | NoRec.US"
  description="FOIA records, camera observations, Policy 450, retention, audits, and ALPR findings in Boone County, Illinois."
>
<main class="page_shell">
  <nav class="jurisdiction_breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/illinois/">Illinois</a><span>→</span><strong>Boone County</strong>
  </nav>

  <header class="article_header">
    <p class="eyebrow">LOCAL SURVEILLANCE · BOONE COUNTY, ILLINOIS</p>
    <h1>Boone County</h1>
    <p class="article_deck">County-level records are kept separate from municipal systems. A camera located inside a city is not automatically counted as a city-owned camera, and Belvidere's municipal inventory is tracked on its own page.</p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">MUNICIPALITIES · OFFICIAL BOUNDARIES</p>
    <h2>Drill down from Boone County to the municipality.</h2>
    <p>The map shows incorporated municipal boundaries intersecting Boone County. Cross-county municipalities are clipped to the Boone County outline on this map, but their municipal dossier applies to the municipality as a whole unless a source says otherwise.</p>

    <div class="map_legend" aria-label="Municipality map legend">
      <span><i class="legend_swatch legend_covered"></i><strong>Research available</strong></span>
      <span><i class="legend_swatch legend_open"></i><strong>Unresearched</strong></span>
      <span><i class="legend_swatch legend_cross_county"></i><strong>Crosses county line</strong></span>
    </div>

    <CountyMunicipalityMap county="Boone" municipalities={booneMunicipalities} />

    <div class="jurisdiction_cards municipality_directory">
      {booneMunicipalities.map(municipality => (
        <a href={`/illinois/counties/boone/cities/${municipality.slug}/`}>
          <strong>{municipality.name}</strong>
          <span>{municipality.form.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + municipality.form.slice(1)} · {municipality.status === 'documented' ? 'Municipal dossier available' : 'Research needed'}{municipality.crossCounty ? ` · also in ${municipality.counties.filter(c => c !== 'Boone').join(', ')} County` : ''}</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>

    <p class="map_note">Municipality inventory is cross-checked against Census and Boone County materials. Boundary geometry is loaded from the Illinois DNR municipal/county GIS layers. <a href={booneMunicipalitySource.censusUrl}>Census place index</a> · <a href={booneMunicipalitySource.countyUrl}>Boone County community data</a> · <a href="https://maps.dnr.illinois.gov/geoservices/rest/services/BaseLayers/MapServer/23">Illinois DNR municipal boundaries</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="evidence_box">
    <span class="status_label">LATEST LOCAL RECORDS</span>
    <h2>{booneCameraInventoryTotals.active} installed · {booneCameraInventoryTotals.planned} planned in the source inventory</h2>
    <p class="map_note">These counts are a records-derived inventory, not live telemetry. BCSO Policy 450 was released June 3, 2026; Belvidere's camera-location release is tracked separately on the municipal page. Future records can supersede these counts.</p>

    <div class="table_wrap">
      <table class="deflock_table compact">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Jurisdiction</th><th>Installed</th><th>Planned</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {booneCameraInventorySummary.map(row => (
            <tr>
              <td>{row.agency}</td>
              <td><strong>{row.active}</strong></td>
              <td>{row.planned}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Total</strong></td>
            <td><strong>{booneCameraInventoryTotals.active}</strong></td>
            <td><strong>{booneCameraInventoryTotals.planned}</strong></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">INVENTORY · BCSO FOIA RECORDS · BELVIDERE FOIA RECORDS</p>
    <h2>What the Boone County Sheriff's Office policy says.</h2>
    <div class="finding_grid">
      <article><strong>Vehicle attributes</strong><p>The policy describes detection of plates together with vehicle make, model, color, and unique identifiers.</p></article>
      <article><strong>Search predicate</strong><p>The policy states reasonable suspicion or probable cause is not required before using an ALPR system itself during authorized operations; enforcement still requires an independent lawful basis.</p></article>
      <article><strong>Alert verification</strong><p>Officers are directed to verify alerts and vehicle information rather than treating an ALPR hit alone as sufficient enforcement justification.</p></article>
      <article><strong>Flock retention</strong><p>The policy states Flock-hosted data is purged after 30 days.</p></article>
      <article><strong>County retention</strong><p>ALPR data downloaded to the county server should be stored no longer than one year, subject to evidence and records-retention requirements.</p></article>
      <article><strong>Auditing</strong><p>The Sheriff or designee is to audit ALPR detection-browsing inquiries at least once per calendar year, including a random sample.</p></article>
      <article><strong>Auditable access</strong><p>The policy describes individual credentials and system use capable of being fully audited.</p></article>
      <article><strong>Immigration restriction</strong><p>The policy states data will not be shared by the county or its contractors/subcontractors for federal immigration-enforcement purposes involving specified federal immigration agencies.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <PublicRecords records={booneCountyRecords} />

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">SUPPORTED / NOT SUPPORTED</p>
    <h2>What the records support — and what they do not.</h2>
    <div class="deflock_split">
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">SUPPORTED</span>
        <ul>
          <li>BCSO uses Flock Safety ALPR technology and has its own county inventory separate from Belvidere's municipal inventory.</li>
          <li>The BCSO policy describes capture of more than the plate itself.</li>
          <li>The policy permits ALPR use without requiring reasonable suspicion or probable cause merely to operate/query the system in the authorized context described.</li>
          <li>Alert verification is required before enforcement action.</li>
          <li>Flock-hosted retention is described as 30 days.</li>
          <li>County-side downloaded data can remain up to one year under the policy, with exceptions for evidence/retention obligations.</li>
          <li>Annual browsing audits are required by policy.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">NOT YET ESTABLISHED</span>
        <ul>
          <li>Exact field-confirmed installation matching for every current mapped coordinate.</li>
          <li>That ICE has direct access for immigration enforcement; the supplied policy says the opposite for that purpose.</li>
          <li>That an officer may lawfully stop a vehicle solely because an ALPR alert occurred; the policy requires verification and a lawful basis.</li>
          <li>Which agencies currently receive Boone County ALPR data.</li>
          <li>How many users currently have system access.</li>
          <li>What the annual audits actually found.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">FOLLOW-UP</p>
    <h2>Records still worth obtaining.</h2>
    <ul class="about_questions">
      <li>Results of annual audits and any corrective actions.</li>
      <li>Current sharing and authorized-agency lists.</li>
      <li>Detection-browsing usage totals and access-log details.</li>
      <li>Authorized-user counts and training records.</li>
      <li>County retention schedules governing exported ALPR records.</li>
      <li>Current contracts, pricing, renewals, and grants.</li>
      <li>Installation dates and exact device-to-coordinate matching.</li>
      <li>Regional or inter-agency search-access agreements.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
